d for multiplication. <|User|>Thank you for walking me through all these methods. Can you also show me how to solve this using the grid method? <｜Assistant｜> <think>.\nCertainly! The grid method, also known as the box method, is a visual and systematic way to multiply two numbers by breaking them down into their place values and then multiplying each part. Let's solve \\(317 \\times 996\\) using the grid method step by step.\n\n1. **Set up the grid:**.\n   - Draw a 3x3 grid because we are multiplying a 3-digit number by a 3-digit number.\n   - Label the top row with the digits of 317 and the left column with the digits of 996.\n\n```.\n  3 | 1 | 7.\n---------.\n9 |   |   |.\n9 |   |   |.\n6 |   |   |.\n---------.\n```.\n\n2. **Write the digits of 317 along the top row and the digits of 996 along the left column:**.\n   - Write 317 along the top row.\n   - Write 996 along the left column.\n\n```.\n  3 | 1 | 7.\n---------.\n9 |   |   |.\n9 |   |   |.\n6 |   |   |.\n---------.\n```.\n\n3. **Multiply each digit in the top row by each digit in the left column:**.\n   - For the top left cell (3 x 9):.\n     ```.\n     3 | 1 | 7.\n     ---------.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     6 |   |   |.\n     ---------.\n     27.\n     ```.\n   - For the top middle cell (3 x 9):.\n     ```.\n     3 | 1 | 7.\n     ---------.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     6 |   |   |.\n     ---------.\n     27.\n     ```.\n   - For the top right cell (3 x 6):.\n     ```.\n     3 | 1 | 7.\n     ---------.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     6 |   |   |.\n     ---------.\n     18.\n     ```.\n   - For the middle left cell (1 x 9):.\n     ```.\n     3 | 1 | 7.\n     ---------.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     6 |   |   |.\n     ---------.\n     9.\n     ```.\n   - For the middle middle cell (1 x 9):.\n     ```.\n     3 | 1 | 7.\n     ---------.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     6 |   |   |.\n     ---------.\n     9.\n     ```.\n   - For the middle right