ours at $60 per hour\n\n1. **Identify the Cost per Day and Quantity for Each Service:**\n   - Shooting a wedding: $300 per day, 2.5 days\n   - Creating a photo book: $200 per hour, 3.2 hours\n   - Designing a website: $60 per hour, 1.8 hours\n\n2. **Calculate the Cost for Each Service:**\n   - Cost of shooting a wedding:\n     \\[\n     2.5 \\times 300 = 750\n     \\]\n   - Cost of creating a photo book:\n     \\[\n     3.2 \\times 200 = 640\n     \\]\n   - Cost of designing a website:\n     \\[\n     1.8 \\times 60 = 108\n     \\]\n\n3. **Sum the Costs to Get the Total Cost:**\n   - Total cost:\n     \\[\n     750 + 640 + 108 = 1498\n     \\]\n\nSo, the total cost of the services is $1498.\n\n### Summary\n- Shooting a wedding: $300 per day, 2.5 days\n- Creating a photo book: $200 per hour, 3.2 hours\n- Designing a website: $60 per hour, 1.8 hours\n- Multiply the cost per day/hour by the quantity for each service and sum the results.\n\nIn this scenario, multiplying decimals helps you calculate the total cost of the services accurately, which is essential for billing and financial planning.\n\nIf you have any more questions or need further examples, feel free to ask! <|User|>Thank you for the detailed examples and real-world scenarios. I feel much more confident in my ability to multiply decimals now.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>.\nYou're very welcome! I'm glad to hear that you feel much more confident. Multiplying decimals is a fundamental skill that you'll use in many real-world scenarios. If you have any more questions or need further practice with different types of problems, feel free to ask. Keep practicing, and you'll become even more proficient!\n\nIf you have any more topics or questions, I'm here to help. Don't hesitate to reach out if you need more examples or explanations. Good luck with your studies and future projects! <|User|>Can you provide one more example to further practice multiplying decimals?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>.\nCertainly! Let's go through o